{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"2","amends":"files","what":"Edited two sims outside FILES: fleet/tests/test_run_engine_reuse.mjs and fleet/tests/test_worker_kata_env.mjs. Each counted `getIssue` calls over the whole run to assert 'exactly one read per task'; both now count only the reads that precede the run's first worker dispatch.","why":"M1 and M2 require fresh `getIssue` calls inside the wave (the Setup read predates every worker, so it cannot carry a fact a worker wrote). Those two clauses are about the SETUP read — the one that checks the revision and takes the fact sheet, and the one the worker's KATA_REF short id comes from — which is what their own prose says; measuring them over the whole run made them fail for a read they were never about. Without this edit the tree would carry two red sims.","id":"01M2MDRAD000006NXQ00HZPN93","ts":1789539396000}
{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"2","amends":"files","what":"Added a `findings` key to each `report.json` task row (`tasks[].findings`, `[]` when the task collected none), carrying the blocking handshake findings M2/M5 raise.","why":"M2 requires the finding to be visible and routed like any blocking finding; the report row is where a task's verdict data already lives, and `skills/ultrapowers/references/report-format.md` declares no `additionalProperties`, so the new key cannot fail a schema check.","id":"01M2MDRAD00001JTK0RRPH73K8","ts":1789539396000}
